WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:05.500
Good news, horror fans: 2018 is shaping up
to be a banner year for spooky and spine-tingling

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:06.520
video games.

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:11.019
From groundbreaking zombie shooters to vampire
RPGs, there's something for every fright fan

00:00:11.019 --> 00:00:12.050
in the new year.

00:00:12.050 --> 00:00:16.190
Here's a look at some of the most promising
— and chilling — titles so far.

00:00:16.190 --> 00:00:17.930
Overkill's The Walking Dead

00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:22.690
Like The Walking Dead's zombie hordes, Overkill's
The Walking Dead is proving very, very hard

00:00:22.690 --> 00:00:24.190
to put down for good.

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:29.289
First announced in 2014 with a message from
Walking Dead creator Robert Kirkman, the first-person

00:00:29.289 --> 00:00:33.640
survival shooter from the studio behind the
Payday series was originally scheduled for

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:35.090
a 2016 release.

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:39.860
Now it looks like The Walking Dead will finally
shamble onto Xbox One, PlayStation 4, and

00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:43.329
PC in the second half of 2018—fingers crossed.

00:00:43.329 --> 00:00:47.800
Because Overkill's The Walking Dead promises
not to be your run-of-the-mill zombie shooter.

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:52.899
It challenges players to survive the zombie-ridden
wasteland using a combination of action, stealth,

00:00:52.899 --> 00:00:54.170
and resource management.

00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:58.240
And like Rick Grimes and his followers, you
won't be going it alone, either—while you

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:01.540
can play solo, cooperative multiplayer will
be the main focus.

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:06.220
"I'm happy to say that it is the, uh, co-op
game that all The Walking Dead fans have been

00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:07.220
waiting for."

00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:09.049
State of Decay 2

00:01:09.049 --> 00:01:11.100
Need more zombie action in the new year?

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:15.159
State of Decay 2 is sure to please Walking
Dead fans — especially those that enjoy

00:01:15.159 --> 00:01:17.829
the survivalist aspects more than the gore.

00:01:17.829 --> 00:01:22.109
Like the first game in the series, State of
Decay 2 forgoes active zombie hunting and

00:01:22.109 --> 00:01:26.670
asks you stay put, hunker down, and build
a base that can protect you and your followers

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:28.219
from the undead horde.

00:01:28.219 --> 00:01:32.599
That's easier said than done, and every choice
you make has lasting consequences.

00:01:32.599 --> 00:01:36.689
You'll need seeds and equipment to grow a
garden and feed your crew, for example, which

00:01:36.689 --> 00:01:41.469
means leading excursions into town to secure
supplies ... which means facing swarms of

00:01:41.469 --> 00:01:42.469
zombies.

00:01:42.469 --> 00:01:44.659
Maybe you should focus on building a guard
tower instead?

00:01:44.659 --> 00:01:45.659
It's up to you.

00:01:45.659 --> 00:01:48.739
That kind of variation is what makes State
of Decay 2 so compelling.

00:01:48.739 --> 00:01:50.689
You'll never play the same game twice.

00:01:50.689 --> 00:01:55.119
Look for this Xbox One and Windows 10 exclusive
in Spring of 2018.

00:01:55.119 --> 00:01:56.799
Metro Exodus

00:01:56.799 --> 00:02:01.389
The Metro franchise doesn't have the name
recognition of games like Dead Space or Bioshock,

00:02:01.389 --> 00:02:06.840
but 2018's Metro Exodus — available on Xbox
One, PlayStation 4, and PC — might change

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:07.840
that.

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:11.210
In a post-apocalyptic world where nuclear
fallout has forced humanity to retreat to

00:02:11.210 --> 00:02:15.790
underground subway tunnels to survive, players
fight their way out of a mutant-filled Moscow

00:02:15.790 --> 00:02:18.849
and cross the continent in search of a better
future.

00:02:18.849 --> 00:02:22.819
Like the previous two games in the series,
players still need to engage in meticulous

00:02:22.819 --> 00:02:27.849
stealth-based challenges and fast-paced combat
to survive, and gathering vital supplies is

00:02:27.849 --> 00:02:29.920
still a big part of the experience.

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:34.819
But Exodus shakes things up by combining linear
levels with new, open areas for players to

00:02:34.819 --> 00:02:35.819
explore.

00:02:35.819 --> 00:02:38.000
Bloodstained: Ritual of the Night

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:42.850
If you miss those traditional 2D Castlevania
games Konami used to crank out out a regular

00:02:42.850 --> 00:02:47.329
clip, longtime Castlevania producer Koji Igarashi
has you covered.

00:02:47.329 --> 00:02:51.650
His Bloodstained: Ritual of the Night isn't
an official Castlevania game, but it might

00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:52.650
as well be.

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:57.110
Like Castlevania, Bloodstained stars a cursed
protagonist who explores a spooky castle filled

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:58.980
with demons and secrets.

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:03.480
You'll amass a wide array of weapons and face
all kinds of monstrous foes in your journey,

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:07.849
while robust RPG-like levelling and crafting
systems will ensure that Bloodstained never

00:03:07.849 --> 00:03:08.849
gets old.

00:03:08.849 --> 00:03:13.110
And yes, while Bloodstained is a Kickstarter-backed
game, which have disappointed in the past,

00:03:13.110 --> 00:03:17.439
don't let that turn you off: Igarashi and
his crew say they purposefully delayed the

00:03:17.439 --> 00:03:22.719
cross-platform, crowdfunded title until 2018
in order to make sure Bloodstained: Ritual

00:03:22.719 --> 00:03:25.190
of the Night lives up to its potential.

00:03:25.190 --> 00:03:26.190
Code Vein

00:03:26.190 --> 00:03:28.829
Mix Dark Souls with vampires, and what do
you get?

00:03:28.829 --> 00:03:30.150
Okay, well, Bloodborne.

00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:34.269
Throw in some anime-inspired art, however,
and you end up with Code Vein, an upcoming

00:03:34.269 --> 00:03:39.970
horror-action title from Bandai Namco, available
on Xbox One, PlayStation 4, and PC.

00:03:39.970 --> 00:03:45.459
Code Vein wears its influences on its sleeve—producers
aren't shy about evoking the Souls comparison,

00:03:45.459 --> 00:03:46.459
and why should they be?

00:03:46.459 --> 00:03:50.510
Dark Souls' combat is just as thrilling as
it is difficult, and you'd be hard pressed

00:03:50.510 --> 00:03:52.969
to find a better model for an action-RPG.

00:03:52.969 --> 00:03:56.859
But Code Vein isn't just a knockoff—and
that's where the vampire element comes in.

00:03:56.859 --> 00:04:00.560
Players can suck their enemies' blood and
then use the super-charged fluid to unleash

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:05.239
special attacks, buff their characters' stats,
and access all kinds of other supernatural

00:04:05.239 --> 00:04:06.239
powers.

00:04:06.239 --> 00:04:07.450
Days Gone

00:04:07.450 --> 00:04:10.920
If you've ever watched Sons of Anarchy and
thought it'd be better with monsters, then

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:12.310
Days Gone is for you.

00:04:12.310 --> 00:04:17.329
The upcoming PlayStation 4 exclusive details
the adventures of a biker-gang-turned-survivalist

00:04:17.329 --> 00:04:22.280
group in the Pacific Northwest in an open-world
adventure that takes cues from Tomb Raider,

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:24.620
Grand Theft Auto, and The Last of Us.

00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:29.490
As Deacon St. John, you'll traverse the decimated
Pacific Northwest's varied terrain on foot

00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:34.650
and by motorcycle, attacking enemy outposts
while making sure your gang remains on top.

00:04:34.650 --> 00:04:36.680
The monsters will make that difficult.

00:04:36.680 --> 00:04:40.900
Set two years after a plague ravished the
Earth and killed most of humanity, the world

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:43.621
of Days Gone is filled with zombie-like creatures
called Freakers.

00:04:43.621 --> 00:04:46.530
Freakers aren't your typical undead foes,
either.

00:04:46.530 --> 00:04:50.470
They don't just shamble or shuffle; sometimes,
they run—and they're really fast.

00:04:50.470 --> 00:04:55.389
In addition to many human enemies, St. John
will need to outmaneuver and dispatch swarms

00:04:55.389 --> 00:04:59.750
of hundreds of Freakers, all while making
sure he's got the resources he needs to fight

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:00.860
another day.

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:05.139
While the specifics of Days Gone's story remain
elusive, the technology on display in the

00:05:05.139 --> 00:05:10.110
demos alone is undeniably impressive, making
this one of the most anticipated titles of

00:05:10.110 --> 00:05:11.840
the first half of 2018.

00:05:11.840 --> 00:05:16.169
Plus, it's likely the only game of the year
to feature a weaponized grizzly bear …

00:05:16.169 --> 00:05:18.380
"Just back up, nice and slow.

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:21.420
Don't make a sound."

00:05:26.240 --> 00:05:27.240
Thanks for watching!

00:05:27.250 --> 00:05:30.120
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:32.509
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

